# AGENTS.md (Project)

Rules for coding agents in `<slug>` (<1-2 sentences on what this project does>). Humans start at `README.md`.

## Tasks (`mise.toml`)

Git hooks and CI call the same `mise` tasks (Python <python_major_minor>+ via `uv`):

- `mise run install` — `uv sync --locked` (malware-checked) + git hooks.
- `mise run format` — `ruff` (imports + format) and `dprint`.
- `mise run check` — `check:local` (`ruff`, `ty`, `deptry`, `dprint`, `betterleaks`, `validate-pyproject`) + `check:network` (`uv audit`).
- `mise run test` — offline `pytest` (`pytest-socket` loopback-only, 60s timeout, 85% branch coverage).
- `mise run build` — `uv build --clear` + strict Zensical API docs (`mise run serve:docs` previews).
- `mise run watch` — continuous test/app watcher.
- **Fast inner loop**: `uv run --locked pytest -q <path>::<test>`, `uv run --locked pytest -q -x -l --lf`, `uv run --locked ruff check <path>`, `uv run --locked ty check <path>`; finish with full `mise` gates.

## Done & Conventions

- Done requires clean `mise run format`, `check`, `test`, and `build` locally, plus tests for changed behavior. Fix root causes — never weaken assertions, add skips/`xfail`s, loosen types, or suppress lints to force green.
- Chain specific exceptions (`raise ... from err`); never swallow errors or log secrets.
- Validate external inputs/settings at boundaries, document defaults and precedence, declare only used dependencies, use modern Python annotations (`list[str]`, `X | Y`, `Annotated`), and write Conventional Commits without attribution.

## Layout

- `src/<package>/`: package exports (`__init__.py`, `__version__`) and cohesive domain modules.
- `tests/`: deterministic offline tests (`@pytest.mark.integration` opt-in only when needed).
- `pyproject.toml`, `mise.toml`, `lefthook.yml`, `dprint.json`: single sources of truth for config and pins.
